# Per-customer manifests are produced by `assemble_scaffold.py --input ...` as
# `<customer>.manifest.jsonc`. They are NOT ignored: a real deploy package
# committed under customer/ must carry its exact manifest for provenance,
# alongside its input.json and rendered package/ (all three are committable —
# see ../NOTICE.md). Scratch `--check` experiments simply show as untracked in
# `git status`; don't `git add` the ones you don't mean to keep.
#
# (This dir previously ignored `*.manifest.jsonc` / `*.manifest.json`; that
# singled the manifest out from its already-committable siblings and is dropped.)
